ften as deliciously perceptible , as the combination of the most exquisite voices with the most perfect modulation , is to the ear . To the last hour of her mortal existence , that smile , and the scene where it was _ uttered _ , were engraved on the heart of Elinor . It announced at once a spirit , that , like the ancient statue , answered every ray of light that fell on it with a voice of melody , and blended the triumph of the glories of nature with the profound and tender felicities of the heart . They spoke no more during the remainder of their walk , but there was more eloquence in their silence than in many words . * * * * * *
